 "notes": "Observed 95% CL exclusion on the axion decay constant from non-observation of periodic variations in 12 yr of JRC 3H decay data (oscillating QCD theta angle). Curve traced from the vector red 'Tritium decay' boundary in Fig. 3 (Figure_3_updated.pdf of the e-print), axes calibrated to the plot frame; reported as 1/f_a [GeV^-1] vs m_a [eV]. Endpoints reproduce the quoted f_a < 9.4e12 GeV at m_a=1.7e-23 eV and f_a < 1.8e10 GeV at 8.7e-21 eV. Jagged frequency-by-frequency limit downsampled to 100 log-spaced points by log-log interpolation. Paper assumes rho_DM = 0.45 GeV/cm^3 (Eq. 12), matching the compilation convention, so no rescaling applied. Future-experiment curves ('12yr' and '1day' fiducial cases) are projections and were excluded.",
